  "question": {
    "text": "The maximum area of a right angled triangle with hypotenuse $h$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "rg9Ra",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{h^2}{2 \\sqrt{2}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JYj5O",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{h^2}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4NTda",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{h^2}{\\sqrt{2}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JmR8F",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{h^2}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let base $=b$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/mge2TNH4GJMxZxcICG5WkqmSl_BA-XMfLFcVlcRlV4g.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nAltitude (or perpendicular) $=\\sqrt{h^2-b^2}$ Area, $\\mathrm{A}=\\frac{1}{2} \\times$ base $\\times$ altitude $=\\frac{1}{2} \\times b \\times \\sqrt{h^2-b^2}$ $\\Rightarrow \\frac{d \\mathrm{~A}}{d b}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\sqrt{h^2-b^2}+b \\cdot \\frac{-2 b}{2 \\sqrt{h^2-b^2}}\\right]$ $=\\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\frac{h^2-2 b^2}{\\sqrt{h^2-b^2}}\\right]$\nPut $\\frac{d \\mathrm{~A}}{d b}=0, \\Rightarrow b=\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{2}}$\nMaximumarea $=\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{h}{\\sqrt{2}} \\times \\sqrt{h^2-\\frac{h^2}{2}}=\\frac{h^2}{4}$",
    "image": null
  },
